@startuml 03-pods-y-conexion
title Pods por namespace y comandos para conectarse

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
left to right direction

package "kube-system" as ns_kubesystem {
  component "coredns (x2)" as coredns
  component "etcd, kube-apiserver,\nkube-controller-manager,\nkube-scheduler" as controlplane
  component "kube-proxy (x4, uno por nodo)" as kubeproxy
}

package "calico-system" as ns_calico {
  component "calico-node (x4)" as calico_node
  component "calico-kube-controllers" as calico_ctrl
  component "calico-typha" as calico_typha
  component "csi-node-driver (x4)" as calico_csi
  component "whisker, goldmane" as calico_obs
}

package "tigera-operator" as ns_tigera {
  component "tigera-operator" as tigera
}

package "kubernetes-dashboard" as ns_dash {
  component "dashboard-web/api/auth/\nkong/metrics-scraper" as dash_pods
}

package "metallb-system" as ns_metallb {
  component "controller" as mlb_ctrl
  component "speaker (x4, uno por nodo)" as mlb_speaker
}

package "rook-ceph" as ns_rook {
  component "rook-ceph-operator" as rook_op
  component "mon-a / mon-b / mon-c" as rook_mon
  component "mgr-a" as rook_mgr
  component "osd-0 / osd-1 / osd-2" as rook_osd
  component "mds-myfs-a" as rook_mds
  component "rook-ceph-tools (toolbox)" as rook_tools
  component "CSI cephfs/rbd\nctrlplugin + nodeplugin" as rook_csi
}

package "wordpress" as ns_wp {
  component "Pod wordpress\n(3 contenedores:\nwordpress+mariadb+redis)" as wp_pod
}

package "default" as ns_default {
  component "nginx-app (prueba)" as nginx_pod
}

note right of ns_wp
  ** Conectarse al Pod de WordPress **
  kubectl -n wordpress get pod -l app=wordpress
  kubectl -n wordpress exec -it deploy/wordpress -c wordpress -- bash
  kubectl -n wordpress exec -it deploy/wordpress -c mariadb  -- bash
  kubectl -n wordpress exec -it deploy/wordpress -c redis    -- sh

  ** Probar cada contenedor **
  kubectl -n wordpress exec deploy/wordpress -c mariadb -- \
    mariadb-admin ping -h 127.0.0.1 -uroot -p'RootK8sLab2026!'
  kubectl -n wordpress exec deploy/wordpress -c redis -- redis-cli ping
end note

note right of ns_rook
  ** Toolbox de Ceph (estado del cluster) **
  kubectl -n rook-ceph exec deploy/rook-ceph-tools -- ceph -s
  kubectl -n rook-ceph exec deploy/rook-ceph-tools -- ceph osd tree
  kubectl -n rook-ceph exec deploy/rook-ceph-tools -- ceph fs status myfs

  ** Logs del operador si algo falla **
  kubectl -n rook-ceph logs deploy/rook-ceph-operator --tail=200
end note

note right of ns_dash
  ** Token de acceso al Dashboard de Kubernetes **
  kubectl -n kubernetes-dashboard create token admin-user
end note

note right of ns_metallb
  ** Diagnostico si el LoadBalancer no asigna IP **
  kubectl -n metallb-system get pods -o wide
  kubectl -n metallb-system logs deployment/controller --tail=100
  kubectl -n metallb-system describe ipaddresspool k8s-lab-pool
end note

note bottom of ns_default
  ** Comando generico para entrar a cualquier Pod **
  kubectl -n <namespace> get pods
  kubectl -n <namespace> exec -it <pod> -- sh
  kubectl -n <namespace> logs <pod> -c <contenedor> --tail=100
end note

legend right
  |= Termino / Tecnologia |= Que es |
  | Namespace | Particion logica dentro de un cluster Kubernetes para agrupar y aislar recursos (ej. wordpress, rook-ceph) |
  | Pod | Unidad minima ejecutable de Kubernetes; puede contener uno o varios contenedores que comparten red y almacenamiento (ej. el Pod wordpress con 3 contenedores) |
  | kubectl exec | Comando para ejecutar un proceso (ej. una shell) dentro de un contenedor de un Pod ya corriendo |
  | CoreDNS | Servidor DNS interno del cluster; resuelve nombres de Service (ej. wordpress.wordpress.svc) a IPs internas |
  | Calico | Plugin de red (CNI) que provee la red de Pods y las politicas de red del cluster |
  | Tigera operator | Operador que instala y gestiona Calico usando el CRD Installation en vez de manifiestos sueltos |
  | MetalLB | Load-balancer software que asigna IPs tipo LoadBalancer en clusters sin proveedor cloud |
  | Rook | Operador que despliega y gestiona el cluster Ceph (mon/mgr/osd/mds) dentro de Kubernetes |
  | Toolbox (rook-ceph-tools) | Pod auxiliar con el cliente ceph instalado, usado solo para diagnostico/administracion manual del cluster Ceph |
  | Deployment | Objeto de Kubernetes que gestiona un conjunto de Pods identicos (replicas, rollout, rollback) |
  | Kubernetes Dashboard | Interfaz web oficial de Kubernetes para ver y administrar el cluster desde el navegador |
endlegend

@enduml
